# SanAntonioSafe Android API Guide

Backend API guide for the SanAntonioSafe Android app.

The backend is role-based. Use the section that matches the signed-in user's role:

- `resident` - reports incidents, uploads photos, receives alerts.
- `responder` - sees assigned incidents and updates response status.
- `barangay_officer` - manages incidents in their barangay and sends alerts.
- `command_center_staff` - manages incident operations and dashboard data.
- `admin` - full system management, users, reference data, settings.

In some notes, "respondent" means `responder`.

## Base Setup

Development base URLs:

| Android target | Base URL |
| --- | --- |
| Android emulator | `http://10.0.2.2:3000` |
| Physical phone on same Wi-Fi | `http://<your-pc-lan-ip>:3000` |
| Production | your deployed HTTPS URL |

Protected endpoints require a Better Auth bearer token:

```http
Authorization: Bearer <session-token>
Content-Type: application/json
```

For `multipart/form-data` photo upload, do not manually set `Content-Type`; let OkHttp set the boundary.

Common error response:

```json
{
  "error": "Validation failed",
  "details": {}
}
```

## Auth APIs

All roles use the same Better Auth endpoints.

| Method | Endpoint | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/sign-up/email` | Create account |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/sign-in/email` | Log in |
| `GET` / `POST` | `/api/auth/get-session` | Validate stored token |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/sign-out` | Log out |

Sign in example:

```bash
curl -X POST http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/auth/sign-in/email \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"user@example.com","password":"password123"}'
```

Android stores the returned session token securely and sends it as:

```kotlin
fun authedRequest(url: String, token: String): Request.Builder =
    Request.Builder()
        .url(url)
        .header("Authorization", "Bearer $token")
```

