## Resident APIs

Residents can create reports, upload evidence photos after sync, view their own reports, and read alerts/notifications.

| Method | Endpoint | Resident use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST` | `/api/incidents` | Create incident while online |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents` | List own incidents |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents/{id}` | View own incident details |
| `PATCH` | `/api/incidents/{id}` | Edit own pending incident |
| `POST` | `/api/incidents/{id}/photos` | Upload local photo after incident exists |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents/{id}/photos/{photoId}` | Download protected photo |
| `GET` | `/api/alerts` | Read targeted alerts |
| `POST` | `/api/alerts/{id}/read` | Mark alert read |
| `GET` | `/api/notifications` | Read notifications |

Create incident body:

```json
{
  "clientReportId": "local-report-uuid-1",
  "clientCreatedAt": "2026-07-04T03:00:00.000Z",
  "incidentCategoryId": "fire",
  "title": "House fire",
  "description": "Smoke seen near the road",
  "latitude": 12.412,
  "longitude": 124.279,
  "locationAccuracy": 8,
  "approximateAddress": "Ward I near municipal road",
  "barangayId": "brgy-ward-i",
  "severityLevel": "critical"
}
```

Important: do not put image data in `POST /api/incidents`. Create/sync the incident first, then upload photos with multipart form data.

Resident offline flow:

1. Store report locally with `clientReportId`.
2. Store photos locally with `clientPhotoId` and the same local report ID.
3. When online, send report JSON using `POST /api/mobile/sync`.
4. Read `serverId` from the sync result.
5. Upload each queued photo to `POST /api/incidents/{serverId}/photos`.
6. Pull updates with `GET /api/mobile/sync?since=<lastServerTime>`.

## Responder APIs

Responders see only incidents assigned to their responder profile. They can view details/photos and update status for assigned incidents.

| Method | Endpoint | Responder use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents` | List assigned incidents |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents/{id}` | View assigned incident details |
| `GET` | `/api/incidents/{id}/photos/{photoId}` | Download protected photo for assigned incident |
| `PATCH` | `/api/incidents/{id}/status` | Update assigned incident status |
| `GET` | `/api/mobile/sync` | Pull assigned incidents and notifications |
| `GET` | `/api/notifications` | Read assignment/status notifications |

Status update body:

```json
{
  "status": "responding",
  "remarks": "Responder team is on the way"
}
```

Allowed incident statuses:

- `pending`
- `verified`
- `assigned`
- `responding`
- `resolved`
- `archived`
- `rejected`

Responder notes:

- A responder cannot assign themselves through the API.
- A responder cannot see unassigned incidents unless they also have a staff/admin role.
- A responder can update status only for incidents assigned to their responder record.

