## Local Photo Uploads

Photos are stored locally on the backend, not Cloudinary. The Android app stores photos locally while offline, then uploads them after the incident exists on the server.

`POST /api/incidents/{incidentId}/photos`

Request type: `multipart/form-data`

Fields:

- `file` - image file
- `clientPhotoId` - stable UUID for the local photo

Allowed MIME types:

- `image/jpeg`
- `image/png`
- `image/webp`

Default max size: 5 MB. Server env override: `MAX_INCIDENT_PHOTO_BYTES`.

Curl example:

```bash
curl -X POST http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/incidents/server-incident-id/photos \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <session-token>" \
  -F "clientPhotoId=local-photo-uuid-1" \
  -F "file=@C:/path/to/photo.jpg;type=image/jpeg"
```

Kotlin/OkHttp upload example:

```kotlin
val body = MultipartBody.Builder()
    .setType(MultipartBody.FORM)
    .addFormDataPart("clientPhotoId", clientPhotoId)
    .addFormDataPart(
        "file",
        "incident.jpg",
        photoFile.asRequestBody("image/jpeg".toMediaType())
    )
    .build()

val request = Request.Builder()
    .url("$baseUrl/api/incidents/$incidentId/photos")
    .header("Authorization", "Bearer $token")
    .post(body)
    .build()
```

Upload response:

```json
{
  "duplicate": false,
  "photo": {
    "id": "server-photo-id",
    "incidentReportId": "server-incident-id",
    "clientPhotoId": "local-photo-uuid-1",
    "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
    "bytes": 123456,
    "sha256": "...",
    "downloadUrl": "/api/incidents/server-incident-id/photos/server-photo-id"
  }
}
```

Retry rule: sending the same `clientPhotoId` for the same incident returns the existing photo with `duplicate: true`.

Protected photo download:

`GET /api/incidents/{incidentId}/photos/{photoId}`

This route requires the bearer token. If using Coil or Glide, configure the image request to include the auth header.

```kotlin
val request = Request.Builder()
    .url("$baseUrl$downloadUrl")
    .header("Authorization", "Bearer $token")
    .get()
    .build()
```

## Offline Sync Details

`POST /api/mobile/sync`

Supported operation types:

- `create_incident`
- `update_profile`
- `register_device`

Push body:

```json
{
  "clientBatchId": "batch-uuid-1",
  "deviceId": "android-device-id",
  "operations": [
    {
      "clientOperationId": "op-uuid-1",
      "type": "create_incident",
      "payload": {
        "clientReportId": "local-report-uuid-1",
        "clientCreatedAt": "2026-07-04T03:00:00.000Z",
        "incidentCategoryId": "fire",
        "title": "House fire",
        "description": "Smoke seen near the road",
        "latitude": 12.412,
        "longitude": 124.279,
        "barangayId": "brgy-ward-i",
        "severityLevel": "critical"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Sync response:

```json
{
  "serverTime": "2026-07-04T03:01:00.000Z",
  "duplicateBatch": false,
  "results": [
    {
      "clientOperationId": "op-uuid-1",
      "type": "create_incident",
      "status": "created",
      "serverId": "server-incident-id",
      "clientReportId": "local-report-uuid-1"
    }
  ]
}
```

Pull updates:

`GET /api/mobile/sync?since=2026-07-04T03:01:00.000Z`

Returns:

- `serverTime`
- `reference`
- `incidents`
- `incidentPhotos`
- `alerts`
- `alertRecipients`
- `notifications`

Store `serverTime` locally and use it as the next `since` cursor.

## Role Access Summary

| API group | Resident | Responder | Barangay officer | Command staff | Admin |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Auth/profile/device/reference | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| Create own incident | yes | supported | supported | supported | supported |
| View incident | own only | assigned only | allowed barangay | staff scope | all staff/admin scope |
| Upload/view incident photos | own incident | assigned incident | allowed incident | allowed incident | allowed incident |
| Update incident status | no | assigned only | yes | yes | yes |
| Assign responders | no | no | yes | yes | yes |
| Send alerts | no | no | yes | yes | yes |
| Dashboard APIs | no | no | yes | yes | yes |
| `/api/admin/*` CRUD | no | no | no | no | yes |

## Environment Needed

Minimum `.env`:

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://san_antonio_safe:san_antonio_safe_password@localhost:5432/san_antonio_safe"
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="change-this-to-a-long-random-secret"
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS="http://localhost:3000,http://10.0.2.2:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BASE_URL="http://localhost:3000"
LOCAL_UPLOAD_DIR="storage/uploads/incidents"
MAX_INCIDENT_PHOTO_BYTES="5242880"
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON_BASE64=""
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@example.com"
```

For a physical phone, add your PC LAN URL to `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`, for example `http://192.168.1.20:3000`.
